# Production safety: every VITE_* value is public and may enter browser bundles.
# Never set VITE_NEON_DATABASE_URL, VITE_DATABASE_URL, database passwords,
# Supabase service-role keys, or migration credentials in frontend configuration.
# Even a read-only PostgreSQL URL contains reusable database credentials.
# The retired Neon/Supabase browser adapters intentionally ignore all env values.

# Configure database secrets/bindings only in the Cloudflare server environment.
# If a server adapter needs DATABASE_URL, provision it as a server-side secret,
# not a VITE_* variable. D1 uses a server-side binding, not a browser URL.
# Keep real values out of this example, source control, build logs, and responses.
# Previously exposed credentials require server-side review/rotation by the owner.

# Browser contract (same origin, GET only): /api/health and /api/data-status.
# These report status only; they do not accept SQL or arbitrary table queries.
# Legacy query methods reject with CLIENT_DATABASE_DISABLED in serverAPI mode.
# Missing/unavailable endpoints reject; they never stand in for empty datasets.
# Vite alone does not provide these endpoints; use the Cloudflare API deployment.
# A successful health response does not establish database/migration readiness.
# Preserve the original site/source data; migration is a separate server workflow.

# App URL used by deployment previews and callbacks if needed.
APP_URL="https://exbeam.com"
